---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const { locale } = Astro.props;

const pageTitle = "Termos e Condições | Luis Ferreira Transferências e Serviços";
const pageDescription = "Page Description";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle} pageDescription={pageDescription} bodyClass="secondary-page">
  <section class="cmp-hero-section" aria-labelledby="hero-section">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--tablet-48">
      <div class="hero__text-container">
        <h1 id="hero-section" class="cmp-hero-heading">
          Terms and Conditions
        </h1>

        <ol class="terms-list">
          <li>
            <h2>Introduction and Acceptance of Terms</h2>
            These Terms and Conditions govern access to and use of the website operated by Luis Ferreira, including the
            booking, coordination and promotional services offered through the website. By accessing the website,
            submitting a booking request or purchasing a service, you agree to these Terms and Conditions. If you do not
            agree, you should not use the relevant services. Any mandatory rights granted to consumers under applicable
            law remain unaffected.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Business Information</h2>
            This website is operated by Luis Ferreira, with registered address at Rua dos Pescadores 117, Portugal. The
            business can be contacted by email at lfdsf57@gmail.com or by telephone at +351 966 831 360. Business
            registration details, tax identification number and any applicable professional licences shall be provided
            where legally required.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Scope of Services</h2>
            The website provides information, booking facilities and coordination relating to passenger transfers and
            shuttle services, residential and holiday property cleaning, and the advertising and promotion of rental
            properties. The precise nature of each service, including whether it is supplied directly by Luis Ferreira
            or by an independent third-party provider, will be indicated where applicable. Separate service-specific
            conditions may apply to individual bookings or agreements.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Bookings and Confirmation</h2>
            Submitting an enquiry, quotation request or booking form does not, by itself, guarantee the availability of
            a service or constitute confirmation of a reservation. A booking becomes confirmed when the applicable
            provider or authorised representative expressly confirms the booking and communicates any relevant price,
            schedule and conditions. Customers are responsible for checking the accuracy of the information supplied
            before submitting a request.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Prices, Quotations and Additional Charges</h2>
            Prices shall be communicated clearly before a customer becomes contractually committed to a booking. Unless
            expressly stated otherwise, a quotation applies only to the services, dates, locations and requirements
            specified in that quotation. Additional services, changes to the original request, waiting time, additional
            cleaning requirements or other chargeable circumstances may incur additional fees, provided these are
            disclosed and agreed in accordance with applicable law. Any applicable taxes and mandatory charges shall be
            included or clearly identified as required by law.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Payments and Deposits</h2>
            Payment methods, payment deadlines, deposits and any outstanding balances shall be communicated during the
            booking process or in the relevant service agreement. Customers must pay the amounts properly due under
            their confirmed booking. No additional payment shall be imposed without an applicable contractual or legal
            basis. Refunds, where due, shall be processed in accordance with the relevant cancellation terms and
            applicable law.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Passenger Transfers and Shuttle Services</h2>
            Transfer bookings are subject to the confirmed itinerary, pickup and destination details, travel date,
            agreed time, passenger numbers and luggage requirements. Customers must provide accurate information, flight
            details where applicable, and a valid contact number. Any applicable transport conditions shall be
            communicated by the responsible transport operator. Where transport is supplied by an independent licensed
            operator, that operator is responsible for performing the transport service to the extent provided by law
            and the applicable agreement. Nothing in these Terms excludes any responsibility legally imposed on Luis
            Ferreira or any transport operator.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Passenger Responsibilities and Delays</h2>
            Passengers must arrive at the agreed pickup point on time and follow reasonable safety instructions given by
            the driver. Customers should promptly communicate flight changes, delays, changes to passenger numbers or
            difficulties locating the pickup point. Waiting periods, missed pickups, additional journeys and associated
            charges shall be governed by the conditions disclosed at the time of booking. No charge shall apply unless
            it has a valid contractual or legal basis. The handling of flight delays and missed connections shall depend
            on the confirmed service conditions.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Transfer Cancellations and Amendments</h2>
            Requests to cancel or amend a transfer must be submitted through the contact details provided on the website
            or in the booking confirmation. Any applicable cancellation deadlines, fees, refund conditions and amendment
            restrictions shall be communicated before the booking is finalised. Where a cancellation or change is
            requested by the provider, the customer shall be informed as soon as reasonably practicable and offered the
            remedies or alternatives required by the applicable agreement and law. Mandatory passenger rights shall not
            be excluded or restricted.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Cleaning Services</h2>
            Cleaning services are performed according to the scope, property type, schedule and requirements agreed at
            the time of booking. Customers must provide accurate information regarding the property's location, size,
            condition, access arrangements and any special cleaning requirements. Services outside the agreed scope,
            including intensive cleaning, excessive soiling, post-construction cleaning or additional tasks, may require
            a revised quotation and the customer's agreement before work proceeds.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Access to Properties and Cleaning Cancellations</h2>
            Customers or property representatives must ensure that the cleaner can safely access the property at the
            agreed time and that necessary access instructions are provided in advance. Customers must disclose relevant
            hazards, restricted areas and any special handling requirements. If access is unavailable or the property
            materially differs from the information supplied, the provider may need to reschedule or revise the agreed
            scope, subject to applicable law and the terms communicated in advance. Cleaning cancellations, rescheduling
            fees and refunds shall follow the conditions disclosed before confirmation and any mandatory consumer
            rights.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Rental Property Advertising and Promotion</h2>
            The website may feature and promote a specific rental property on behalf of its owner. This may include
            property descriptions, photographs, amenities, location information, availability, rental prices and contact
            or booking enquiries. The purpose of this service is to present the property to prospective guests and
            facilitate enquiries regarding potential stays. Advertising the property does not guarantee enquiries,
            reservations, occupancy levels or rental income.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Rental Property Information and Responsibilities</h2>
            The property owner is responsible for ensuring that all information supplied for publication is accurate,
            complete and up to date, including descriptions, photographs, amenities, availability, rental prices and
            occupancy conditions. The owner is also responsible for ensuring that the property is legally authorised for
            its intended rental use and that any required registrations, licences, insurance and other legal obligations
            are fulfilled. Unless expressly agreed otherwise in writing, the website acts solely in the capacity agreed
            with the owner and does not itself assume the owner's responsibilities as landlord or accommodation
            provider.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Property Content and Advertising Updates</h2>
            The website operator may update, correct or remove property information where reasonably necessary,
            including where details are inaccurate, outdated, misleading or no longer relevant. The property owner must
            promptly communicate any material changes to the property's availability, rental prices, facilities,
            conditions or legal status. Photographs, descriptions and other materials supplied by the owner may be used
            to promote the property through the website and related marketing channels to the extent authorised by the
            owner. Any agreed advertising fees, promotional arrangements or additional services shall be governed by the
            relevant agreement between the parties.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Third-Party Providers and External Services</h2>
            The website may refer customers to or coordinate services supplied by independent transport operators,
            cleaning professionals, property owners, accommodation providers, payment processors or external websites.
            Where a third party supplies a service under its own contract, its applicable service conditions may also
            apply. The role of Luis Ferreira in each transaction shall be explained clearly where relevant. Nothing in
            these Terms excludes responsibility for services, representations or obligations for which Luis Ferreira is
            legally responsible.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Customer Information and Communications</h2>
            Customers must ensure that all personal and booking information supplied through the website is accurate and
            up to date. Information may be used to process enquiries, confirm reservations, coordinate services,
            communicate changes, handle payments and fulfil legal obligations, in accordance with the applicable Privacy
            Policy. Customers should not submit personal information relating to other individuals unless they are
            authorised to do so or another lawful basis applies.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Privacy and Data Protection</h2>
            Personal data shall be processed in accordance with applicable data protection legislation, including the
            General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and relevant Portuguese law. Further information about the
            categories of personal data collected, purposes of processing, legal bases, recipients, retention periods
            and individuals' rights shall be provided in the website's separate Privacy Policy. Where required, consent
            shall be obtained before using non-essential cookies or similar tracking technologies.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Website Availability and Accuracy</h2>
            Reasonable efforts are made to keep the website available and its information accurate and current. However,
            uninterrupted availability, error-free operation and the permanent accuracy of all third-party information
            cannot be guaranteed. Information displayed on the website may change as service availability, prices,
            schedules and property details are updated. Confirmed contractual arrangements and mandatory legal rights
            shall take precedence over general website information where applicable.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
            Unless otherwise stated, the website's original text, design, branding, graphics and other materials are
            owned by or lawfully licensed to Luis Ferreira and are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.
            They may not be reproduced, distributed, modified or commercially exploited without prior authorisation,
            except where permitted by law. Users submitting photographs, descriptions or other advertising material
            confirm that they have the necessary rights and permissions for its intended use.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Prohibited Use</h2>
            Users must not use the website for unlawful purposes, submit fraudulent or misleading information, infringe
            third-party rights, interfere with website security or functionality, distribute malicious software, or
            attempt unauthorised access to systems or data. Luis Ferreira may take reasonable and lawful measures to
            restrict access, investigate suspected misuse or remove unlawful content.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Liability and Force Majeure</h2>
            Nothing in these Terms excludes or limits liability where such exclusion or limitation is prohibited by law.
            Subject to that restriction, Luis Ferreira shall be responsible for its own acts, omissions and contractual
            obligations in accordance with applicable law. Neither the business nor a service provider shall be treated
            as automatically liable for circumstances genuinely beyond reasonable control, such as severe weather,
            natural disasters, government restrictions or major transport disruptions; however, any applicable duties to
            notify customers, mitigate disruption, provide refunds or offer remedies remain unaffected.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Complaints and Dispute Resolution</h2>
            Customers who wish to raise a complaint should contact Luis Ferreira using the contact details published on
            the website, providing their booking reference and a description of the issue. Complaints will be reviewed
            and addressed within a reasonable period. Where required by Portuguese law, information concerning the Livro
            de Reclamações (Complaints Book) and the competent alternative dispute resolution entity shall be made
            available. Consumers retain any rights to seek assistance from competent authorities or courts.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Amendments to These Terms</h2>
            Luis Ferreira may update these Terms and Conditions to reflect changes in its services, business operations
            or applicable law. The current version and its effective date shall be published on the website. Changes
            shall apply prospectively, subject to applicable law and any existing contractual commitments. Changes to a
            confirmed booking or an existing agreement shall not be imposed retrospectively where this is not legally
            permitted.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Severability</h2>
            If any provision of these Terms and Conditions is found to be invalid, unlawful or unenforceable, the
            remaining provisions shall continue in effect to the extent permitted by law. The invalid provision shall be
            interpreted or replaced only to the extent necessary to achieve a lawful result consistent with the original
            purpose, without diminishing mandatory consumer rights.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Applicable Law and Jurisdiction</h2>
            These Terms and Conditions shall be governed by Portuguese law, subject to any mandatory consumer protection
            rules that apply. Any dispute shall be submitted to the competent court determined under applicable law.
            Nothing in this clause removes a consumer's right to bring proceedings before a court that has jurisdiction
            under mandatory applicable rules.
          </li>

          <li>
            <h2>Contact Information</h2>
            For questions about these Terms and Conditions, bookings, cleaning services or complaints, please contact
            Luis Ferreira at lfdsf57@gmail.com or +351 966 831 360. Please include any relevant booking or service
            reference to help us respond efficiently.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .terms-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-left: 1rem;
    list-style: decimal;
    max-width: 60ch;

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
